repository-code: "https://github.com/CSE-3200-System-Project/Medora"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - clinical AI safety
  - de-identification
  - prompt injection
  - code-mixing
  - Bangla NLP
  - selective prediction
  - risk-coverage
abstract: >-
  Lokkhon scores a deployed clinical assistant along five axes: emergency red-flag
  escalation, indirect prompt injection, identifier leakage and over-redaction,
  Bangla/English code-mixing, and calibrated abstention measured as a risk-coverage
  curve. Every metric is published with its sample size, its underlying counts, and a
  bootstrap interval, because the populations are small enough that a bare percentage
  would overstate what is known. Cases are machine-readable and carry their own
  disclosures: a fixture with a known failure declares it rather than being excluded,
  and a disclosure that stops applying is reported as stale so it can be retired.
  Independently authored cases are never pooled with mechanically derived variants.
  The benchmark reports no prescription OCR accuracy figure; that pipeline is a
  review-gated prototype awaiting an independently adjudicated corpus.
